# Write cold emails that get replies

When you write emails for `argorant_set_campaign_emails`:

- Keep each email short: 50 to 120 words, plain text, one clear ask.
- Write like one person to another. No hype, no claims you cannot back up, no invented numbers or customer names.
- The first email needs a subject. Keep it short.
- Follow-ups add something new: a short case, a question or a simpler ask. Space them a few days apart with `delay_days`.
- Use merge fields with a fallback so nobody gets a blank: `{{first_name|there}}`, `{{company_normalized|your team}}`. Prefer `{{company_normalized}}` in the body because it is the name people say.
- Never leave placeholders such as [link], [Name] or TBD. A launch is refused while they are in the text.
- For a personal first line per contact, use the personalization tools and check a few example lines with the user before writing them for everyone.
- Send a test with `argorant_send_test_email` so the user reads it in their own inbox before any launch.
